== a break on a word loop header ends the loop with its variable bound:
v=1
== a break on a body command runs that command and ends the loop:
body-1
tail
== a continue on a body command skips the rest of that iteration:
body-1
body-2
body-3
tail
== a continue on a word loop header skips every body:
v=3
== an inner header continue leaves the outer body running:
outer-A
after-inner
outer-B
after-inner
tail
== an inner header break leaves the outer loop running:
outer-A
after-inner
outer-B
after-inner
tail
== a break on a while condition ends the loop:
n=0
== a break on an arithmetic init clause runs the clause and ends the loop:
i=0
== a break on a case header ends the loop before the case runs:
tail
== an exit in an action abandons the traced command:
rc=7
